      3px, 3py, 3pz, 4s, 3dxy, 3dxz, 3dyz, 3dz^2, 3dx^2-y^2,rotatable,
      animation">
    <meta content="Page design and layout by J. Gutow 5-2006, page
      written by perl script orbtohtml.pl" name="details">
    <meta content="This page is designed to have the text and normal
      html edited in a standard web design" name="instr1">
    <meta content="program. The javascript is to control the jmol applet
      (see below). It is best to use" name="instr2">
    <meta content="the perl scripts to generate the proper java script
      to allow orbital display. It is" name="instr3">
    <meta content="important to have all the gzipped files in the same
      directory as the .html file. The" name="instr4">
    <meta content="files needed are: 1) a gzipped file with the atom
      coordinates, in any of the formats Jmol" name="instr5">
    <meta content="can read. 2) a gzipped gaussian cube file for each of
      the orbitals to be displayed. To" name="instr6">
    <meta content="save loading time it seems to be better to avoid
      including the atom coordinates in the" name="instr7">
    <meta content="cube files. It is also recommended that the file
      names for the surfaces correspond to" name="instr8">
    <meta content="reasonable names for the orbitals as the file names
      are used to generate the menu items" name="instr9">
    <meta content="that appear in the popup menus for selecting
